# Packages of the userland image (userland/Containerfile). Several per line are fine; # starts a
# comment. Try a package in the playground box first, then add it here.

# What distrobox-init installs on a box's first start (distrobox 1.8.2.5, setup_pacman; mlocate is
# gone from Arch). The image has them, so a new box skips that setup (/.containersetupdone).
# zsh: the user's shell. Not its glibc-locales: the Containerfile generates the hosts' locales
zsh bash-completion bc curl diffutils findutils glibc gnupg iputils inetutils
keyutils less lsof man-db man-pages mtr ncurses nss-mdns openssh pigz pinentry procps-ng rsync
shadow sudo tcpdump time traceroute tree tzdata unzip util-linux util-linux-libs vte-common wget
words xorg-xauth zip mesa vulkan-intel vulkan-radeon

# Fonts (cached at build time) and the keyring of [cachyos]. JetBrains Mono is the host's: distrobox
# mounts its fonts and /etc/fonts/local.conf in the boxes.
# ttf-liberation: Chromium (Brave, VS Code) only takes a metric-compatible font for Arial/Helvetica
# (and its default sans-serif, Arial); without one, a page that lists "Noto Color Emoji" got its
# digits and spaces from the emoji font, spread out (Syncthing's GUI, 2026-10-11)
fontconfig cachyos-keyring noto-fonts-emoji ttf-liberation

# Desktop apps, exported to the host by distrobox.ini
# Brave Origin from [aur]: Brave's minimal edition, its extras compiled out
brave-origin-bin pipewire-pulse libpulse
# Microsoft's VS Code from [aur]: the Dev Containers extension (work projects) does not work in
# Code-OSS or VSCodium. podman is a client of the host's socket (99-remote.conf)
visual-studio-code-bin podman git
# adw-gtk-theme: the GTK3 theme darkman switches between light and dark on the host (shared dconf).
# gvfs: GIO's client of the host's gvfs daemon (smb:// in Thunar); the daemon and its backends
# (gvfs-smb) are the host images' (sway layer)
thunar gvfs adw-gtk-theme
# remote-viewer: the screen of test VMs (iso/test-vm, VNC or SPICE with sound)
virt-viewer
# QEMU for the throwaway test VMs (iso/test-vm, iso/test-install): KVM, OVMF and QEMU's user
# networking work in the box; the bootc images have no virtualization since 2026-10-20. The
# virtio-vga module (test-vm's screen) needs the virtio-gpu one, which Arch does not declare:
# without it QEMU 11.1.2 segfaulted
qemu-base edk2-ovmf qemu-hw-display-virtio-vga qemu-hw-display-virtio-gpu
gimp imagemagick
# imv: image viewer, default for images in the boxes (mimeapps.list); also exported to the host
imv
# mpv: video and audio player, default for both in the boxes (mimeapps.list); exported
mpv
# Syncthing, and squeezelite from [aur] (a Lyrion player; ffmpeg linked in, which mpv needs
# anyway): run by host user units that enter this box (dotfiles)
syncthing squeezelite

# Terminal tools
neovim btop fzf zsh-completions
# note export (dotfiles scripts/.local/bin/note): Markdown to PDF; typst finds any installed font,
# where groff's ms only has its own (no ☐ ☒ for task lists, no PNG images). pandoc-bin from [aur]:
# upstream's binary, where Arch's pandoc-cli brings 238 packages, most of them Haskell libraries
pandoc-bin typst
# ansible-core, not ansible (500 MiB of collections): a project installs what its requirements.yml
# lists
ansible-core ansible-lint
